  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-06-14T02:43:12.034Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As VRChat has just introduced its item system, it may still be trying to find its footing and determine what to and not to allow, and how to provide, items going forward.\n\nAs part of this, I suggest VRChat add the ability for items to **be marked as \"player only\".**\n\nWhat this means is:\n\n- Player-Only Items are *only* visible *to their owner,* **regardless of any safety settings.**\n\n- Player-Only Items may access an additional set of properties of their owner, via Udon & Soba, which may not be available with \"public\" items.\n\n- Player-Only Items may attach themselves to the player HUD, provide additional utility, interact with the VRC Camera, etc. via Udon & Soba, which most certainly **would not be available to normal items.**\n\n- Player-Only Items **cannot** interact with other players.\n\nThe intent of these features would allow VRChat, and potentially users in the event of UGC, to **provide new \"utility\" items, similar to the VRChat camera or VRC Player Mirror,** which aim to enhance the functionality of the VRChat client.\n\nExisting systems, such as the camera and mirror, could even theoretically be migrated to such an improved system, providing a uniform way of spawning objects, **whether or not they are local to the spawning user.**\n\nOther possible enhancements could be to provide a separate subsection, similar to the \"Exclusive\" item sections in Stickers & Emoji, for \"My Tools\", with a subheading of \"Visible only to you\", where these Player-Only Items would be stored.",
